<header><p class="st-kicker">electorate · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Electorate of Trier</h1><p class="st-meta">898 CE – 1803 CE (approx.) · capital Koblenz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The ecclesiastical principality of the archbishops of Trier, one of the seven electors of the Holy Roman Empire, stretching along the Moselle and Rhine.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a> had been an imperial capital in late Roman times and a bishopric since the 3rd century. In 898 King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwentibold">Zwentibold</a> granted Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radbod-of-trier">Ratbod</a> immunity and comital rights over the city, the basis of the archbishops' temporal power. Over the following centuries they built a territory along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moselle">Moselle</a> from Trier to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koblenz">Koblenz</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Archbishop Baldwin of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-luxembourg">Luxembourg</a>, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-vii-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Henry VII</a>, consolidated the territory between 1307 and 1354. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull of 1356</a> confirmed the archbishop as an elector and arch-chancellor for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Burgundy</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> moved their residence to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koblenz">Koblenz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ehrenbreitstein-fortress">Ehrenbreitstein</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a> kept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-robe">Holy Robe</a> relic, exhibited to pilgrims.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-occupation-of-the-netherlands">French revolutionary armies</a> occupied the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> in 1794. The last elector, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clemens-wenceslaus-of-saxony">Clemens Wenceslaus of Saxony</a>, fled, and in 1803 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichsdeputationshauptschluss">Reichsdeputationshauptschluss</a> dissolved the electorate, its remaining eastern lands going to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-nassau-weilburg">Nassau-Weilburg</a>. After 1815 most of it became Prussian.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/electorate-of-trier.jpg" alt="Electorate of Trier" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: ZH2010 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_St_George%27s_Cross.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>898 CE – 1803 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>electorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Koblenz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ratbod, Baldwin of Luxembourg, Clemens Wenceslaus of Saxony</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Moselle Franconian German, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/luxembourg">Luxembourg</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Archbishopric of Trier, Kurtrier</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1350&amp;focus=electorate-of-trier" aria-label="Electorate of Trier on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4833 445 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Electorate of Trier lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5153 701L5199 691M5153 701L5229 694M5153 701L5054 728M5153 701L5147 688M5153 701L5153 701"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5199 691h0M5229 694h0M5054 728h0M5147 688h0M5153 701h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5153 701h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5153 701h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a